Haah's three-dimensional cubic code has no string-like logical
  operators and possesses a logarithmic energy barrier.  Under Davies
  dynamics, Bravyi and Haah proved a low-temperature lifetime bound of the
  form
  \begin{equation}
    T_{\mathrm{mem}}\ge L^{c\beta}
    \quad\text{for some $c>0$, but only when}\quad
    L\le L^\star\sim e^{\beta/3}.
    \label{eq:p9-cubic-code-lifetime}
  \end{equation}
  Because the admissible size in Eq.~\eqref{eq:p9-cubic-code-lifetime} is
  bounded at fixed $\beta$, the cubic code is partially self-correcting but
  does not satisfy Eq.~\eqref{eq:p9-self-correction-condition}
  \sourcecite{ref:p9-bravyi-haah}{BH13}.

